    .help = Let the Decision-Making Agent stand in at the decision points this agent reaches, whatever the workspace's switch says
cli-arg-agent-add-effort =
    .help = How hard the plan's models work: auto (the Decision-Making Agent names the level per task) | minimal | low | medium | high | xhigh | max, fitted to what each model takes. Omit it, or say inherit, and the `agents.effort` setting decides
cli-arg-agent-add-harness =
    .help = Harness this agent runs on (see `bisa harness list`)
cli-arg-agent-add-mcps =
    .help = MCP registry id (repeatable). See `bisa mcp list`
cli-arg-agent-add-models =
    .help = A model for the plan, best-first (repeatable), as `id[=weight][@effort][: what it suits]` and quoted, since `[1m]` is a glob to a shell: `--model "claude-opus-5-5[1m]=3@max: design work"`. See `bisa agent models <harness>`
cli-arg-agent-add-prompt =
    .help = System prompt text (or use --prompt-file)
cli-arg-agent-add-prompt_file =
    .help = Read the system prompt from a file
cli-arg-agent-add-respond =
    .help = Who may direct this agent: owner-only (default) | members
