    .about = Live harness sessions (the runtime roster)
cli-cmd-sessions-abort =
    .about = Terminate a session at once — `aborted` is terminal
cli-cmd-sessions-list =
    .about = List running/parked sessions (the runtime roster)
cli-cmd-settings =
    .about = Settings: three scopes, one registry
cli-cmd-settings-get =
    .about = One key's resolved value
cli-cmd-settings-registry =
    .about = The registry: every key, its kind, default and allowed scopes
cli-cmd-settings-set =
    .about = Write one key at one scope: `machine`, `workspace` or `project`
cli-cmd-settings-show =
    .about = Every key, its value and where it came from
cli-cmd-settings-unset =
    .about = Remove one key from one scope; the value falls back to the next layer
cli-cmd-signal =
    .about = Signals: the durable record of what a workflow's events heard, and the named ones raised by hand
cli-cmd-signal-emit =
    .about = Raise a named signal: heard by the starts, waits and boundary events that name it. Nothing listening is a normal, quiet answer
cli-cmd-signal-list =
    .about = The newest signals, queued or settled — never a payload
cli-cmd-addon =
    .about = Addons: the overlay widgets installed here, and the switches on each
cli-cmd-addon-list =
    .about = List the addons installed here
cli-cmd-addon-show =
    .about = Show one addon: its manifest, its grants, whether it runs
cli-cmd-addon-install =
    .about = Install a built-in from the catalog (`bisa catalog list --kind addon` names them)
cli-cmd-addon-import =
    .about = Import an addon from a folder on this machine
cli-cmd-addon-enable =
    .about = Turn an addon on
cli-cmd-addon-disable =
    .about = Turn an addon off
cli-cmd-addon-remove =
    .about = Remove an addon: its record, its bundle, its snapshot
cli-cmd-addon-grant =
    .about = Grant permissions the manifest declares
cli-cmd-addon-revoke =
    .about = Take permissions back
cli-arg-addon-import-grants =
    .help = Grant a permission the manifest declares (repeatable)
cli-arg-addon-import-enable =
    .help = Turn it on at once
cli-cmd-skill =
    .about = Skills: the shared library of procedures agents follow
cli-cmd-skill-add =
    .about = Add a skill to the library
cli-cmd-skill-edit =
    .about = Change a skill. The id is fixed: agents reference it, and a rename would detach every one of them
cli-cmd-skill-list =
    .about = List the library
cli-cmd-skill-rm =
    .about = Delete a skill. Refused while any agent still carries it — detach it there first (`bisa skill usage <id>` lists them)
cli-cmd-skill-show =
    .about = Show one skill, including its markdown
cli-cmd-skill-usage =
    .about = Which agents carry this skill
cli-cmd-status =
    .about = Show a goal's status, workflow and run — or one run's, by its id
cli-cmd-step =
    .about = One step of a run — a goal's, or a run of the workspace: answer, release, done
cli-cmd-step-answer =
    .about = Answer a waiting `human` step
cli-cmd-step-done =
    .about = A `human` step you did by hand: it is done
cli-cmd-step-release =
    .about = Release a `wait` step a person is holding
cli-cmd-stop =
    .about = Stop a goal: it stops listening, its sessions ended, its queued runs withdrawn, its live run cancelled; the goal stays open, ready for a new run
cli-cmd-tags =
    .about = Tags: the one filing system, and what carries which tag
cli-cmd-team =
    .about = Teams: agents and humans working a goal together
cli-cmd-team-add-member =
    .about = Add a member: --human <pubkey> or --agent <id>
cli-cmd-team-create =
    .about = Create a team (agents + humans working one goal together), when the catalog has no ready-made one that fits (`bisa catalog list --kind team`)
cli-cmd-team-list =
    .about = List teams
cli-cmd-team-remove-member =
    .about = Remove a member: --human <pubkey> or --agent <id>
cli-cmd-team-rm =
    .about = Delete a team. Its members are untouched — a team groups agents, it does not own them — and it is refused while anything still names the team itself (`bisa team usage <id>`)
cli-cmd-team-show =
    .about = Show one team: its members, and the goals it is carrying
cli-cmd-team-usage =
    .about = What still points at this team: assignments, workflows, gate policies
cli-cmd-unassign =
    .about = Take assignees off a goal (no names clears the whole list)
cli-cmd-unread =
    .about = Mark a conversation unread
